  "packageSize": 462298,
  "projectUrl": "https://trobee.one/",
  "published": "2026-10-13T18:38:57.06Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.1: The binaries are now Authenticode-signed by TroBeeONE LLC. Decodes datetime values as DaffyTee 0.3.1 does, rounded to the millisecond as SQL Server shows them (.000, .003, .007), so --approximate writes them as literals SQL Server accepts. DaffyTee 0.3.0 and earlier decoded a datetime after 00:02:23 wrong unless the recording has raw bytes: inspect warns about procedure calls without raw bytes that hold such values, and run --approximate skips them rather than send the wrong time.\n0.1.0: First release. Replays DaffyTee (0.3.0 or later) recordings against a test SQL Server at recorded pace (with --speed), fast or serial; byte-exact from --raw recordings, with transaction descriptors patched and prepared-statement and cursor handles mapped; approximate T-SQL for procedure calls recorded without raw bytes. inspect, target, run, report and compare commands; report.json and a self-contained report.html. Tested with ADO.NET, EF Core, ODBC and JDBC workloads on SQL Server 2022 and 2025.",
